      \field{abstract}{In this paper, the authors investigate the Deep Sea Treasure ({DST}) problem as proposed by Vamplew et al. Through a number of proofs, the authors show the original {DST} problem to be quite basic, and not always representative of practical Multi-Objective Optimization problems. In an attempt to bring theory closer to practice, the authors propose an alternative, improved version of the {DST} problem, and prove that some of the properties that simplify the original {DST} problem no longer hold. The authors also provide a reference implementation and perform a comparison between their implementation, and other existing open-source implementations of the problem. Finally, the authors also provide a complete Pareto-front for their new {DST} problem.}
